idence against that backdrop, so the forecast stays near the combined fundamentals rather than the poll alone.", "watch": "Any independent polling or outside spending surge for Gronli in the final weeks would be the main signal that the race is tightening beyond the current picture.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Open seat: Dusty Johnson (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "South Dakota's at-large House seat is open this cycle after incumbent Dusty Johnson retired to run for governor. Republicans nominated Attorney General Marty Jackley, who won his June primary and has raised about $1.4 million with over $1 million on hand. Democrat Nikki Gronli has raised roughly $260,000 and trails badly in financial resources.\n\nThe state leans about fifteen points Republican, and the only recent poll, sponsored by a Democratic firm, showed Jackley ahead 47 to 43 among likely voters. Prediction markets give Gronli roughly a four percent chance of winning. The combination of the state's lean, the money gap, and market pricing points to a Republican hold, though the sparse polling leaves some room for uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -15.31}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.035, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0242, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0239, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.019, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0299, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0301, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05